{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872440-vampire-in-chicago","id":872440,"title":"Vampire in Chicago?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T09:29:06-07:00","id":872440,"title":"Vampire in Chicago?","content":"I am running a game of Werewolf set in Fuller Park in Chicago. My players have just started, and have managed to corner and destroy a girl vampire. I have a few questions to the vampire savvy here...<br /> <br /> I know that vampire society is not a unified thing. But if said vampire is of some standing in the Prince's court, what things would the prince, or members of the court, do to the PCs? or would they take it out, or with, other werewolves? (Possibly one of the Alpha packs in the city)<br /> <br /> Does anyone here run a vampire game in Chicago? would be interesting to cooperate to some degree on playing the two sides of supernaturals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:34:47-07:00","id":872445,"title":"","content":"You're in luck: Chicago in the only city described for Vampires, Werewolves, /and/ Mages, in the creatively named World of Darkness: Chicago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:44:18-07:00","id":872454,"title":"","content":"I know, and have the PDF, but if possible, It would be nice to cooperate with someone who is running a game set in that city, and possibly make use of his version of the vampires in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T19:11:04-07:00","id":873457,"title":"","content":"What do you want to happen? Vampires are cliquish, catty, and callous, but are quick to recognize most existential threats. If you want your players at war with the vampires, the Prince might get pissed, or her Covenant will. If you want your players engaged in their politics, some rival of your dead vamp might try to sic the pack on another upstart. Plenty of Kindred just want to keep their hunting grounds in peace, and a pack of werewolves can threaten a territory, or protect it in the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> The quick and easy thing is to use the Chicago source book for the setting. Figure out what the repercussions should be for killing this vampire, identify or create the interested parties, and then make life hell for your pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T19:51:25-07:00","id":873479,"title":"","content":"I got some creative mileage (locations, grasp of distances and orientation, touristy factoids, visuals) out of playing Watch Dogs when I was in the process of putting my spin on Chicago by Night. Never having done any actual grown-up research on the city itself I couldn't comment on its accuracy, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 04-24-2016, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:32:10-07:00","id":876056,"title":"","content":"In Chicago there are rules and Vampire Prince Maxwell is meeting with Mages and Werewolves regularly, they all reached an agreement: the Werewolves would have the district around Union Station. If the the Vampire girl was killed in kindred territory, the easiest way for Maxwell would be to claim revenge from the Werewolf's authorities themselves since &quot;rogue werewolves&quot; broke a pact between the two factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T04:10:49-07:00","id":880864,"title":"","content":"Hello Greyskull, we've been playing a vampire chronicle based in Chicago for five years now, on and off. The published material is numerous (WoD:Chicago, the three VtR novels &quot;A Hunger Like Fire&quot;, &quot;Blood In, Blood Out&quot;, &quot;Marriage of Virtue and Viciousness&quot; plus several short stories here and there dealing with Solomon Birch, Prince Max, Old John &amp; co.) and provides a very solid base for ideas. <br /> <br /> In our version of the city, Chicago is a vast metropolis populated by several hundred Kindred. There is enough population to fill all the clan and faction roles (from Primogens, Sheriffs and Hounds to Ordo Kogaion, Dragon Knights, Castellans and Navigators, Lancea Electors and Inquisitors etc etc) and then some - minor factions like Scratch's Machine, Norris' Intelligence Network or the Undercity vampires are important enough to have carved out their unique niches. And of course, there are numerous other supernaturals present, despite being a Requiem-focused chronicle: werewoves, mages, strix, revenants, ghosts, blessed our otherwise unnatural mortals, a full cooking pot of ideas and story hooks that we've used from all sorts of resources. <br /> <br /> I'd be very interested in exploring this idea of expanding the world and the characters together - I've never done collaborative storytelling work before and it could be fun. I've got tons of material on the characters and the city structure lying around: several dozen NPCs in different grades of elaboration, character relation charts, who is who graphs for some major and minor factions, city and influence maps... It's almost too much material and it would be very chaotic if I started just dumping it out. How do you suggest we begin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1745-nox-ascensa","name":"Nox Ascensa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T02:26:55-07:00","id":881608,"title":"","content":"Hey Nox, <br /> <br /> It would be too chaotic to just throw all that at me, but let's do a discussion.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, my players got the north part of Fuller park as their Territory. In the south-west corner of that small place, they managed to get a whiff of a vampire child that was killing off people, causing them to kill themselves, or kill others, and then commit suicide. She wasn't a very powerful vampire, but I figured, being shunned by the larger vampire society, she could be used by Norris in some plot of his, and having the players bring about her death, he came to visit them, himself, after kidnapping the daughter of one of their wolf-blooded.<br /> He got them to agree to back off from attacking any vampire, and apologize for killing her. (but not before a conflict erupted, and he did take some damage).<br /> <br /> Now, i don't know if you wanna slip that into your ongoing game, maybe have your players get a whiff of something like this, but I would be interested to hear your thoughts of how this might play out on the Vampire end. The players have been mildly chastised by the Whispers pack for their behavior.<br /> <br /> I haven't, yet, mapped out much of the werewolves in the city, but I have decided that to the north of their territory, is a pack called the Dancing Lilies, a group of female Werewolves, led by Anastacia &quot;Ice Petals&quot;, who works as an aide to one of the City Councillors.To their east is a pack of Blood Talons, called The Boars. An aggressive bunch who seek to expand their territory, and currently looking to take a stab at the Pure Pack to their south. To the west is The Transits, a pack of Iron Masters. They already had a run in with them, and one of my pack memebrs got slapped with an oath not to hurt another werewolf for a year, since he unjustly attacked one of that pack. And to their South is a Pure pack, who lost some members, and a part of their territory, where my players now have a territory, who are burning for some vengeance.<br /> <br /> And all this, when they got their territory just a mere 3 weeks ago...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:42:36-07:00","id":883118,"title":"","content":"Ah, there is trouble brewing all around your players! Times of opportunity as well, it seems. My Chicago campaign is presently on ice (we're doing a bit of Mage, and then there's loads of good material in Dark Eras I'm dying to try out) so let's focus on your story for a while, from the vampire perspective. <br /> <br /> The South Side is currently a political battleground for the Kindred: for many years, discontent has been brewing in the Carthian Movement, targeted against the leadership of Barowski. The South Side holds a sizeable and organized Carthian population revolving around three assemblies (one of which is controlled by my players' coterie). Prince Max has long been looking for an opportunity to undermine the Carthian unity, and after a recent bloody incident involving a Belial's Brood infestation, he finally managed to turn the South Side Carthians (SSC) openly against the faction leadership. As a result, a large area to the south of Washington Park has been recently granted to the SSC assemblies to run a political egalitarian experiment (the &quot;Experiment&quot;), highly autonomous, completely free of their faction's influence and with the prince's backing. <br /> <br /> This new turn of events has produced considerable shifts in population, power and territory. Many neonates and low-influence vampires started settling in the SSC Experiment zone, considering it &quot;virgin territory&quot; in a city with otherwise well-established power structures. A wild-west attitude has sprung up, aided by the fact that the SSC have not yet refined their patrol and vigilance routines. Other supernaturals enjoy greater liberties in the Experiment, at least until someone begins fucking things up seriously. The mainstream Carthians are hostile against the Experiment and try to undermine it covertly at any opportunity, actively employing all sorts of agents (werewolves included). Meanwhile, Prince Max sits back and enjoys the spectacle.<br /> <br /> The vampire child may well have been under the protection of some SSC vampire, say the Gangrel Julia, an ex-prostitute who now serves as the protector of sex workers in the local red light district and has always had a big heart and compassionate attitude to outcasts. Julia is an elder and well respected in the SSC assemblies but holds no office. Perhaps she's looking to exact vengeance/justice for the child's death using the SSC, but she could also be convinced to turn her attention to those truly behind the killing and not the hitmen. <br /> <br /> A great place to stage werewolf-vampire encounters in the south side is the Zero Club, the new Elysium of the SSC Experiment. No supernatural powers, no feeding, no guns allowed. A three'story venue with private basement and emergency safe havens to those on Zero's (the Daeva owner's) good graces. Main theme: unattainable desire. I could go on and on about this club and the things that happen in there, I should even have a floor plan around somewhere. <br /> <br /> Do your PCs or their adversaries do/deal drugs? There's big commotion lately in west Washington Park, where gang wars have erupted. The Nosferatu Scratch and his mafiosi have tipped the balance by offing a high-ranking trafficker, and the are lots of corpses falling lately and lots of influence up for grabs. The Boars are presumed to be actively involved in the fight, perhaps joining Scratch's Machine, or fighting the mob boss for a big slice of the pie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1745-nox-ascensa","name":"Nox Ascensa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T23:25:58-07:00","id":883512,"title":"","content":"My PCs are considering going into drug trafficking, not yet aware how it will affect the Shadow, or too naive to consider it. <br /> <br /> I have a question. Do you perhaps have a map with the current territories of various vampires? It would be great to see one, with short notes on the residents. I think I will try to work on creating such a map for the werewolf packs, at least those close by to my characters' pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:27:59-07:00","id":883981,"title":"","content":"I don't have a complete map unfortunately - I've thought of doing one several times, but it's an ambitious project considering there are more than 700 vampires in our version of Chicago. I do have a draft version that I started filling just before we switched campaigns, which is totally incomplete but may still serve you somehow: <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?hl=en_US&amp;mid=1Kuhecs-RgqFYN1qhNN1zQSHf8dU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?h...1qhNN1zQSHf8dU</a><br /> <br /> I've identified some major points of interest categorized by faction, as well as some major landmarks, hunting grounds etc. The icons serve as secondary classification. <br /> <br /> Again, it's totally incomplete. Perhaps we could work on this together - I can send you edit rights and you can put in some layers of your own with the werewolf POIs and territories, and over time it may grow into a useful resource!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1745-nox-ascensa","name":"Nox Ascensa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T03:38:16-07:00","id":884508,"title":"","content":"That is cool. I know noting down hunting grounds and havens for 700 vampires is a bit much, and I do not expect such a detailed map, unless you REALLY wanted to do so (I kid).<br /> <br /> But even seeing this map is kinda cool. I started doing a map for my campaign, though luckily, my players haven't met many packs yet, so I do not need to mark out every single pack out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1PWRhWH40LNC3girfuJKik4pJNYg&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1PWRhWH40LNC3girfuJKik4pJNYg&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1PWRhWH40LNC3girfuJKik4pJNYg&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=1PWRhWH40LNC3girfuJKik4pJNYg&amp;usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A collaborative map would be awesome, and maybe we can find people who ran Mage, Changeling, Hunter, Promethean, and Beast, to add their own POIs to the map. It would create a wondrous resource for anyone who would ran a Chicago campaign for CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:26:37-07:00","id":884903,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's way too OCD to map out the entire population! Besides, I tend to make up new characters as I sketch out new stories, and this planning phase progressively enriches the roster.<br /> <br /> The collaborative map idea is great, Chicago seems to have been designed with inter-supernatural conflict in mind - I'm all in. In the case of multiple people playing the same splat we may have some conflicts, as each one's vision is bound to differ significantly. Conflict resolution is not fun (I do it as a day job) so going wide (few people of many game lines) rather than deep (many people of the same line) would work best, I think.<br /> <br /> I guess it deserves a new thread under the generic WoD forum though, don't you agree?<br /> <br /> Please do revise the sharing permissions on your map: as &quot;Everyone with the link&quot;, I don't get view access. I'll send you a request for access if you desire to keep the map private.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1745-nox-ascensa","user":"Nox Ascensa","date":".  syntax 05-07-2016, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1745-nox-ascensa","name":"Nox Ascensa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:40:15-07:00","id":885033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nox Ascensa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872440-vampire-in-chicago?p=883118#post883118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Zero Club, the new Elysium of the SSC Experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to see I'm not the only one who's cribbing from Butcher<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T11:53:07-07:00","id":890057,"title":"","content":"Hey Grey, wanna share your map?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1745-nox-ascensa","name":"Nox Ascensa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:10:52-07:00","id":891220,"title":"","content":"Hey Nox, sent you a private message about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:02:32-07:00","id":891253,"title":"","content":"Hey Nox, sent you a private message about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}